                        "review": "Likely one of the most complete fighting games out there. King of Fighters 2002 is a great game that has quantity AND quality when it comes to its roster, having its own line up of original characters, and guest characters from other SNK fighting games, such as Art of Fighting and Fatal Fury. There's a character for everyone, each one with a different playstyle.\nThe pixel art graphics are just perfet, characters have fluid, detailed and smooth animations, and the backgrounds are lively and full of life, something only SNK could have pulled off at the time.\nGameplay is simple, two buttons for light attacks, two for heavy attacks, and a special one. It's easy to learn, but hard to master. Once you get the hang of a character (well, three characters, since the focus of this game is 3v3 battles), it feels so rewarding. The higher difficulty is for the most part balanced, but it doesn't hold your hand. Online play is nicely executed, but good luck trying to fight the experts in ranked matches. You'll need it.\n\nIn conclusion, THIS is the game that turns people into SNK fans. It's just that good.",
